  <main id="main-content">
    <section id="hero">
      
      <br />

<img src="https://zen-bhabha-c96f6d.netlify.app/images/ron_bronson_800.jpg">

<strong>Current Role</strong>
<p>I currently lead one of the largest in-house design teams in the government, spearheading initiatives in user experience, product & service design, and content strategy. In this role, I:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Drive digital transformation efforts across multiple agencies and departments</li>
  <li>Oversee the development and implementation of user-centered design processes</li>
  <li>Collaborate with cross-functional teams to align design strategy with organizational goals</li>
  <li>Mentor and develop a team of designers, researchers, and content strategists</li>
  <li>Champion accessibility and inclusive design practices in government services</li>
</ul>
</div>

<strong>Professional Experience</strong>
<p>With over 15 years of experience in the digital realm, my career spans various aspects of design, strategy, and digital transformation:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Design Leadership:</strong> Guided design teams in both public and private sectors, fostering cultures of innovation and user-centricity</li>
<li><strong>Service Design:</strong> Pioneered service design methodologies to improve citizen experiences with government services</li>
<li><strong>Digital Strategy:</strong> Developed and implemented digital strategies that bridge user needs with organizational objectives</li>
<li><strong>UX Research:</strong> Conducted and overseen extensive user research to inform design decisions and product strategy</li>
<li><strong>Content Strategy:</strong> Led content strategy initiatives to improve information architecture and user engagement</li>
<li><strong>Accessibility Advocacy:</strong> Championed accessibility in digital products, ensuring inclusive experiences for all users</li>
<li><strong>Design Education:</strong> Taught design courses at the college level, shaping the next generation of designers</li>
<li><strong>Public Speaking:</strong> Delivered talks and workshops on design leadership, service design, and digital transformation at international conferences</li>
</ul>
          <div class="social-wrapper">
